      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I feel like this is two very different changes merged into one which makes it hard to vote for personally. \n\nI absolutely agree we should have a public like/dislike ratio, not having it makes the feature useless to me (even if its tuning some secret recommendation algo behind the scenes). There is a reason that everyone absolutely hated when Youtube removed the public like/dislike. Still to this day I feel the impact of that change on Youtube despite them probably having put more work, time and money into their algorithm systems than any other company on earth.\n\nI don't agree those likes/dislikes should be gated just behind age verification (though it can be an element that is considered), that is a very high bar to clear for a feature like this. Other anti-botting methods can be used to protect those ratios (Choosing if a vote counts based on other analytics like past voting, time spent on platform, friends, etc) just like other platforms do.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
